---
permalink: /cables.html
layout: base.njk
documentTitle: "USB-C Cable Database: Compare Reported Speed & Charging | WhatCable"
description: "Find USB-C cable reports by name, speed, charging rating or identity code. Compare the essentials, then open the technical details."
ogImage: "https://www.whatcable.uk/screenshot.webp"
extraHead: |
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/cable-database/catalog.css">
---
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "@id": "https://www.whatcable.uk/cables#dataset",
  "name": "WhatCable cable fingerprint database",
  "description": "Crowd-sourced USB-C cable e-marker fingerprints reported via WhatCable. Entries record the reported manufacturer and product identifiers, encoded cable capabilities, declared speed and charging rating, with links to the original reports. These are identity reports, not physical performance tests.",
  "url": "https://www.whatcable.uk/cables",
  "dateModified": {{ cabledb.updated | isoDate | dump | safe }},
  "keywords": [
    "USB-C", "USB4", "Thunderbolt", "Thunderbolt 5", "e-marker",
    "USB Power Delivery", "USB-C cable database", "cable VDO", "USB-IF VID"
  ],
  "creator": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Darryl",
    "url": "https://github.com/darrylmorley"
  },
  "license": "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT",
  "isAccessibleForFree": true,
  "distribution": [
    {
      "@type": "DataDownload",
      "encodingFormat": "application/json",
      "contentUrl": "https://www.whatcable.uk/cables.json"
    }
  ]
}
</script>

<main class="cables-page" data-catalog>
  <header class="catalog-heading"><div><span class="catalog-eyebrow">The community cable library</span><h1>Get to know your cable.</h1><p>Find a cable by name or by the identity code shown in WhatCable. Compare its reported data speed and charging rating, then open the details when you need them.</p><p class="catalog-meta">{{ cabledb.count }} entries · Updated {{ cabledb.updated | readableDate }}</p></div><a class="catalog-help-link" href="/inside-a-cable"><strong>Same plug. Different insides. →</strong><span>Explore the 3D diagram to see what the wires and identity chip actually do.</span></a></header>
  <section aria-label="Search and filter cables" class="catalog-controls" id="catalog-controls" hidden>
    <div class="catalog-search-row"><label for="catalog-search">Find a cable<input id="catalog-search" type="search" placeholder="Try Apple, CalDigit, 0x05AC or a report number" autocomplete="off"></label><button type="button" id="catalog-clear" disabled>Reset filters</button></div>
    <div class="catalog-filters"><label for="catalog-speed">Reported data speed<select id="catalog-speed"><option value="">All speeds</option>{% for speed in cablecatalog.speeds %}<option value="{{ speed | escape }}">{{ speed }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label for="catalog-power">Reported charging rating<select id="catalog-power"><option value="">All ratings</option>{% for power in cablecatalog.powers %}<option value="{{ power | escape }}">{{ power }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label><label for="catalog-sort">Sort results<select id="catalog-sort"><option value="name">Cable name · A–Z</option><option value="speed">Highest reported speed</option><option value="power">Highest reported power</option></select></label></div>
  </section>
  <div class="catalog-results-bar"><p id="catalog-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">{{ cabledb.count }} entries</p><a href="#reading-reports">Reported ratings, not performance tests ↓</a></div>
  <noscript><p>All entries are shown below. Use your browser’s Find command to search; each entry’s details still open without JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  <div class="catalog-column-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Cable / report description</span><span>Reported speed</span><span>Reported power</span><span>Details</span></div>
  <section id="catalog-results" aria-label="Cable reports">
  {% for cable in cablecatalog.records %}
    <details class="catalog-record" data-search="{{ cable.search | escape }}" data-name="{{ cable.brand | escape }}" data-speed="{{ cable.speedLabel | escape }}" data-power="{{ cable.powerLabel | escape }}" data-speed-number="{{ cable.speedNumber }}" data-power-number="{{ cable.powerNumber }}">
      <summary class="catalog-summary"><h2 class="catalog-name">{{ cable.brand | escape }}<span class="catalog-id">{{ cable.type | capitalize }} cable · Report {{ cable.issueNum | escape }}</span></h2><span class="catalog-stat"><span class="catalog-stat-label">Reported speed</span><strong>{{ cable.speedLabel | escape }}</strong><small>Data capacity</small></span><span class="catalog-stat"><span class="catalog-stat-label">Reported power</span><strong>{{ cable.powerLabel | escape }}</strong><small>Charging rating</small></span><span class="catalog-open-label">Details</span></summary>
      <div class="catalog-details"><p>These values come from the cable’s identity chip—its digital label. They do not measure the speed or charging power your setup will achieve.</p><h3>The complete report</h3><dl class="catalog-fields"><div><dt>Data declaration</dt><dd>{{ cable.speed | escape }}</dd></div><div><dt>Power declaration</dt><dd>{{ cable.power | escape }}</dd></div><div><dt>Construction reported</dt><dd>{{ cable.type | capitalize }}</dd></div><div><dt>Manufacturer ID · VID</dt><dd><code>{{ cable.vid | default("Not reported", true) | escape }}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Product ID · PID</dt><dd><code>{{ cable.pid | default("Not reported", true) | escape }}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Registered vendor name</dt><dd>{{ cable.vendor | default("Not reported", true) | escape }}</dd></div><div><dt>Encoded capabilities · cable VDO</dt><dd><code>{{ cable.cableVDO | default("Not reported", true) | escape }}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Certification identifier · XID</dt><dd><code>{{ cable.xid | default("Not reported", true) | escape }}</code></dd></div></dl><div class="catalog-source"><a href="{{ cable.issueURL | escape }}">Read original report {{ cable.issueNum | escape }} on GitHub ↗</a><a href="#reading-reports">What do these fields mean?</a></div></div>
    </details>
  {% endfor %}
  </section>
  <div id="catalog-empty" hidden><h2>No matching cable reports</h2><p>Try a shorter name, an identity code, or remove a filter. Not every cable has been reported yet.</p><button type="button" id="catalog-empty-reset">Show all cables</button></div>
  <section class="catalog-notes" id="reading-reports"><div><h2>Read the label. Check the connection.</h2><p>This library collects identity-chip reports from WhatCable users. A familiar name or matching code can help identify a cable, but is not a unique serial number or proof of authenticity.</p><p>A missing manufacturer or certificate alone does not mean a cable is faulty. A compatible passive cable may also carry newer signals faster than its older label suggests. WhatCable compares available reports across the port, cable and connected device to help explain your actual connection.</p><details><summary>Speed, charging and technical terms</summary><p><strong>Mbps / Gbps</strong> describe data capacity; <strong>W (watts)</strong> describes power. More charging power does not mean faster file transfers. The charger and device must also support the power being requested.</p><p><strong>Passive</strong> cables do not boost or rebuild data signals; <strong>active</strong> cables contain electronics that do. Both can have an identity chip.</p><p><strong>VID and PID</strong> identify the reported vendor and product. <strong>VDO</strong> is the encoded capability data. <strong>XID</strong> is a certification identifier, not proof of Thunderbolt certification. “Unregistered” means the vendor ID was not found in the list used here.</p><p>Power values are preserved from the reports, including unusual combinations. A declared voltage/current pair alone does not establish compliance. A 50 V, 5 A cable rating permits a maximum nominal USB Power Delivery contract of 48 V × 5 A = 240 W.</p></details><p><a href="/pro#connection-diagnostics">See how Pro compares the whole connection →</a> · <a href="/cables.json">Download the report data (JSON)</a></p></div><div class="catalog-report"><h2>Help fill in the gaps.</h2><p>Have a cable that is missing from the library?</p><ol><li><a href="/">Get WhatCable</a> and connect your cable.</li><li>Choose <strong>Report this cable</strong> in the app.</li><li>Review the pre-filled GitHub report and submit it.</li></ol><p>Reports appear here after they have been reviewed and added.</p><a href="https://github.com/darrylmorley/whatcable/issues?q=label%3Acable-report">Browse community reports ↗</a></div></section>
</main>
<script src="/assets/cable-database/catalog.js" defer></script>
